\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The missing product on one axis}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{In dimension one the [normalized odd volume](fdip-0179)
is #{\omega=\varepsilon_1}. Take #{S=\mathbb C} with
#{\varepsilon_1=\bbI_S}. Its only volume sign is #{+1}.
In a nonzero axial symbol #{f_1(r)\varepsilon_1} the only
eigenvalue is #{f_1(r)}. Omitting the one axis from the ordered
product leaves the empty product #{\bbI_S}. There is no pair
of transverse directions to turn.}
